# IST Website — Design System & Build Spec

**Use this as project rules for an AI coding agent.**

- **Cursor:** save as `.cursor/rules/ist-design.mdc` (set `alwaysApply: true`) or as `AGENTS.md` at repo root.
- **Kiro:** save as `.kiro/steering/ist-design.md` with front matter `inclusion: always`.
- **One-shot prompt:** paste the whole file, then add: *"Build the homepage first, desktop and mobile, following this spec exactly. Stop and show me before moving to other pages."*

Assume **Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind** unless the repo already says otherwise. Motion via CSS + Intersection Observer; reach for a library only where it earns its weight.

---

## 0. Who the client is and what the site must do

Integrated Switching Technologies (IST) builds resilient networking for environments where connectivity breaks: satellites moving out of view, drones behind terrain, ships past the horizon, robots losing line of sight. Conventional networks treat those interruptions as failures. IST treats them as the operating environment.

Two products ship today — **Locus** (assured data distribution engine) and **Crucible** (mission simulation and validation). Three more stack layers are in development and are deliberately unnamed.

**The site must read as a platform company, not a two-product startup.** Audience is mixed: technical buyers, program leads, investors, and non-technical partners.

**The 10-second test.** Within ten seconds a visitor understands: what problem IST solves, who it serves, why it matters, and what to do next. If a section doesn't move one of those four forward, cut it.

Quality bar and tone reference: `cesiumastro.com`, `spaceapp.org` — dark, mission-critical, serious without being impenetrable. **Do not copy their layouts or identity.** Reference only.

