## 1. HARD CONSTRAINTS — violating any of these fails acceptance

These exist because AI agents reliably invent exactly this kind of content. Do not.

| # | Rule |
|---|---|
| 1 | **No fabricated metrics.** No "99.9% uptime", no "500+ nodes", no counters, no stat bands, no testimonials, no valuations. If a layout wants a number, use the literal token `{{TBD}}` and flag it in your summary. |
| 2 | **No fabricated UI screenshots.** No mock dashboards, no invented telemetry panels, no fake Locus or Crucible interfaces. Use clean illustrated diagrams instead. |
| 3 | **No names for unreleased products.** The hardware, interoperability, and ecosystem layers are unnamed. Do not invent names, specs, or capability copy for them. Approved labels only: `In Development`, `Coming Soon`, `Details coming soon`. |
| 4 | **No email address anywhere on the public site.** Not in the footer, not in schema markup, not in a `mailto:`. All contact routes through the form to a backend address. |
| 5 | **No customer, investor, advisor, partner, or government logos.** No logo wall. No "trusted by" strip. |
| 6 | **No founder bio, name, employer history, or headshot.** Not in this version. |
| 7 | **No fabricated news posts.** Build the News page design and filter system; leave the content array empty with a documented shape. |
| 8 | **No invented features or partnerships.** Only capabilities described in this document. |
| 9 | **Do not generate a logo.** Reference `/public/brand/ist-logo.svg` and leave a placeholder if absent. Never redraw or "improve" the mark. |
| 10 | **Strip all ecommerce artifacts** — cart icons, shop links, product/price schema, checkout routes — if any exist in the starting template. |
| 11 | **Never use the line "the future will not be one giant network."** It contradicts the hardware and interoperability roadmap. |
| 12 | **Copy marked `[LOCKED]` ships verbatim.** You may adjust line breaks. You may not reword. |

When in doubt, say less. Restraint is the brand.

