## 4. Typography

*Designer's call — swap the families if you have a stronger pairing, but keep the roles and the scale.*

| Role | Face | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Display | **Archivo** (variable, use the Expanded width axis at 110–125% for the hero) | Wide industrial grotesque. Reads as signage and instrumentation, not startup-default. Avoids Inter and Space Grotesk, both of which are the category cliché. |
| Body | **IBM Plex Sans** | Engineering heritage, humanist warmth, excellent at 16–18px on dark. |
| Utility | **IBM Plex Mono** | Eyebrows, section numbers, status tags, data labels, the four-step flow keys. |

Load via `next/font` with `display: swap`. Subset latin. Preload the display weight used above the fold.

**Type scale** (fluid via `clamp`, mobile → desktop):

```
Hero      clamp(2.75rem, 7vw, 6.5rem)   Archivo Expanded 700 / 0.94 lh / -0.03em
H1        clamp(2.25rem, 4.5vw, 3.75rem) Archivo 600 / 1.05 lh / -0.02em
H2        clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem)    Archivo 600 / 1.15 lh / -0.015em
H3        clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.5rem)    Archivo 600 / 1.25 lh
Lead      clamp(1.125rem, 1.6vw, 1.375rem) Plex Sans 400 / 1.55 lh / --ist-text-muted
Body      1rem (16px min, never smaller) Plex Sans 400 / 1.65 lh
Small     0.875rem                        Plex Sans 400 / 1.6 lh
Eyebrow   0.75rem                         Plex Mono 500 / 0.14em tracking / UPPERCASE / --ist-text-dim
Tag       0.6875rem                       Plex Mono 500 / 0.1em tracking / UPPERCASE
```

Body copy max width: **68ch**. Lead paragraphs: **54ch**. Never full-bleed text.

Sentence case for headings — not Title Case. Uppercase is reserved for eyebrows and status tags, which is what makes it read as instrumentation.

