## 7. Motion

Deliberate and few. Extra animation is what makes a site read as generated.

| Where | Behavior |
|---|---|
| Scroll reveal | `opacity 0→1`, `translateY 16px→0`, `--dur-slow`, `--ease-out`. Stagger children 60ms. Fires once at 20% visibility. |
| Hero | Headline reveals in two lines, 120ms apart, on load. Support line follows at 400ms. Nothing loops. |
| Parallax | Hero and Vision background images move at ~0.4× scroll speed. `transform` only — never `background-position`. |
| Network diagram | Nodes connect in sequence, packets traverse, dashed links resolve to solid. ~4s, plays once on scroll-in, replays on hover. |
| Stack reveal | Five layers animate in sequentially, 100ms apart, top to bottom. Live layers land solid; in-development layers land dashed. |
| Hover | Buttons and tiles: 180ms border/color shift, ≤2px lift, ≤1.02 image scale. Nothing bouncy, no springs. |

**Mandatory:**

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    scroll-behavior: auto !important;
  }
}
```

Everything must be fully readable and usable with motion disabled. No content that only appears via animation.

