## 8. Mobile & accessibility floor

Mobile is a non-negotiable requirement, not a resize pass.

- Hero headline breaks as **"Every Device." / "Any Network."** — never a single orphaned word.
- Body text ≥16px with ≥1.6 line height. No exceptions.
- Zero horizontal scroll at 320px. Test tables, diagrams, cards.
- Diagrams **simplify** responsively — fewer nodes, stacked layout, larger labels. Do not shrink the desktop SVG.
- Buttons comfortably tappable, not full-bleed.
- Nav overlay contrast checked against `--ist-surface-raised`.
- Logo crisp at phone size — SVG, no raster fallback.
- Stack section reflows to a vertical list with status tags inline.

Accessibility floor: semantic landmarks, one `h1` per page, visible focus ring (`2px solid var(--ist-focus)`, `2px` offset), keyboard-navigable everything, `alt` text on all imagery, decorative SVG `aria-hidden`, forms with real `<label>` elements, AA contrast throughout.

Performance: LCP < 2.5s, CLS < 0.1. `next/image` with explicit dimensions. Lazy-load below the fold. Total JS budget under 200KB gzipped.

